  "verdict": "CENTRE_PRINTING_OVER_LENGTH",
  "claim": "The prespecified contrast is not diagnostic here. Its first term is an index_only change and its second a centre_only change, and the character gaps run the same way, so a prompt-length account and a centre-printing account predict the same sign for it (observed Delta_binding = -0.1497, 95% CI [-0.2591, -0.0391]). The design is a crossed 2x2, so the verdict comes from decomposing the six distances by which feature differs. Changing only whether the bin index is printed moved the operator by 0.301 (2.2 times block noise); changing only whether the numeric bin centre is printed moved it by 0.428 (3.1 times); changing both, 0.454. The centre feature exceeds the index feature by +0.127 (95% CI [+0.047, +0.214], exact sign test p = 0.0113). Within every cell the character gap varies by a factor of 2.6 to 7.8 while the response distance does not move resolvably, so which feature differs predicts the distance and how many characters differ does not. The three distances from the fully labelled condition are monotone in prompt length: taking the other conditions in order of decreasing character gap (458, 374, 315 characters), where a monotone length account requires non-increasing distances, the mean TVs are 0.460, 0.440, 0.312.",
  "primary_interpretation_rule": "Delta_binding is judged on its bootstrap interval. A permutation p is reported but is not read as support for Delta_binding itself, because its null is the absence of any condition effect rather than Delta_binding = 0.",
